@transformcm{1.0}{0.0}{0.0% }{1.0}{15.64897pt}{11.70842pt}\pgfsys@invoke{ }\hbox{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}% \definecolor[named]{pgfstrokecolor}{rgb}{0,0,0}\pgfsys@color@gray@stroke{0}% \pgfsys@color@gray@fill{0}\hbox{\minipage[b]{402.32205pt}\color[rgb]{0,0,0}% \definecolor[named]{pgfstrokecolor}{rgb}{0,0,0}\pgfsys@color@gray@stroke{0}% \pgfsys@color@gray@fill{0}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\small{ f\#\#\# System:}% \par You are a teacher. Given a task, you explain in simple steps what the % task is asking, any guidelines it provides and how to use those guidelines to % find the answer.\par\#\#\# { f Human:} \par You will read a meeting % transcript, then extract the relevant segments to answer the following % question: \par Question: How does Steven feel about selling? \par Here is a meeting transcript: \par---- \par{John}: Alright, so we're all here to discuss the offer we received from % Microsoft to buy our startup. What are your thoughts on this? \par{Lucy}: Well, I think it's a great opportunity for us. Microsoft is a huge% company with a lot of resources, and they could really help us take our % product to the next level. \par{Steven}: I agree with Lucy. Microsoft has a lot of experience in the tech% industry, and they could provide us with the support we need to grow our % business. \par{John}: I see your point, but I'm a little hesitant about selling our % startup. We've put a lot of time and effort into building this company, and I'% m not sure if I'm ready to let it go just yet. \par{Lucy}: I understand where you're coming from, John, but we have to think % about the future of our company. If we sell to Microsoft, we'll have access to% their resources and expertise, which could help us grow our business even % more. \par{Steven}: Right, and let's not forget about the financial benefits. % Microsoft is offering us a lot of money for our startup, which could help us % invest in new projects and expand our team. \par{John}: I see your point, but I still have some reservations. What if % Microsoft changes our product or our company culture? What if we lose control % over our own business? \par{Steven}: You know what, I hadn't thought about this before, but maybe % John is right. It would be a shame if our culture changed. \par{Lucy}: Those are valid concerns, but we can negotiate the terms of the % deal to ensure that we retain some control over our company. And as for the % product and culture, we can work with Microsoft to make sure that our vision % is still intact. \par{John}: But won't we change just by virtue of being absorbed into a big % company? I mean, we're a small startup with a very specific culture. Microsoft% is a huge corporation with a very different culture. I'm not sure if the two % can coexist. \par{Steven}: But John, didn't we always plan on being acquired? Won't this be% a problem whenever? \par{Lucy}: Right \par{John}: I just don't want to lose what we've built here. \par{Steven}: I share this concern too \par---- \par Please answer the following question:\ Question: How does Steven feel about selling?\ Extract from the transcript the most relevant segments for the answer, and % then answer the question.\ \par{ f\#\#\# Orca}: \hbox to11.38pt{\vbox to7.97pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter% \hbox{	hinspace\lower 0.0pt\hbox to0.0pt{\pgfsys@beginscope\pgfsys@invoke{ }% \definecolor[named]{pgfstrokecolor}{rgb}{0,0,0}\pgfsys@color@gray@stroke{0}% \pgfsys@invoke{ }\pgfsys@color@gray@fill{0}\pgfsys@invoke{ }% \pgfsys@setlinewidth{	he\pgflinewidth}\pgfsys@invoke{ }
